Z||000000||86SEFIERO||06-22-2000||05:00 AM||||<BR>How do they sound? What kind of power you feeding them?? What brand subs?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||06-22-2000||09:33 AM||||Putting subs in the rear trunk won't work unless you plan on standing outside the car when you play the stereo. There is no way to get the sound to the inside of the car and no backseat to direct the sound thru like other cars. You'd never hear it with the windows closed or driving down the highway. You might feel the vibrations but that would be the extent of it. ||||reg||13
Z||000002||pHoOl||06-22-2000||10:45 PM||||There is a rear trunk?  They must have forgotten to put one in my GT.  All i have is this little thing that could fit a gallon of milk.  {sorry if sarcasm doesn't travel over bulletin boards, i'm new at this}||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula||06-23-2000||05:34 PM||||I almost put 3 Ameircan bass VFLs in the trunk with a power acoustic 1.6 kw (1600 watts rms) amp in.........but I thought it would shake the car too much and the box would be a b*tch to build.||||reg||1
Z||000004||stimpy||06-23-2000||08:09 PM||||Just wrap your exhaust maifolds wth $100 bills. You'll hear just as much in the cabin and it will cost less.<BR> <BR>Here's an idea... get a Yakima rack on top of your car, get a 30" woofer in a bandpass enclosure ported through your sunroof and fill the trunk with a stack of Marshall amps.<P>Better yet, buy a van.<P>Speakers wil always sound best INSIDE the passenger compartment where there are actual human ears. Since the airspace in Fieros are relatively small, you really don't need all that much speaker to get good sound.  If all you want to do is piss off the neighbors, well, then, what can I say? ||||reg||1
Z||000005||ThatRickGuy||06-23-2000||09:30 PM||||there was some talk of this earlier, basically I think it came down to, if you want to put a sub in the trunk, you would need a bullet proof engine to take the vibrations of the super powerful speakers/amp you'd need to hear it in the cabin...||||reg||1
Z||000006||kinboyatuwo||06-25-2000||08:28 PM||||HEEHEE i found the trunk guys it is between the two pieces of carpets in the back lol<BR>by the way i can fit my kid sister back there if you are looking to put the subs in the back for the second passenger<BR>give er sh!t||||reg||4
Z||000007||Taijiguy||06-27-2000||08:05 AM||||Take the money you'd put into speakers and amps, and apply it to a nice paint job and a nice sounding exhaust. Then get attention with the beautiful appearance and audacious sound of the Fiero rather than the irritating incessant "thump(BZZZZ)THUMP(BZZZZZZ)thump(BZZZZZ)" of speakers turned up too loud revealing how loose your body panels really are.....||||reg||6
Z||000008||80's BOY||06-27-2000||09:17 AM||||i had subwoofers in my trunk...........for about 30 minutes while i was carrying them home from the store!!!!!!!!||||reg||12
Z||000009||jbarnes||06-28-2000||03:18 PM||||I found a couple of bazooka tubes fit quite snugly behind the passenger seat. I origionally had one but it didn't do it for me so I put in a second right on top. Your passenger just losses a little leg room. Sounds great though.||||reg||6
Z||000010||StuGood||06-28-2000||04:55 PM||||Thanks for the great money-saving tip!<P>I'll return the favor, by sharing a tip of my own:  I found the $100 bills would only adhere to my exhaust system if I soaked them in that exhaust-sealer-in-a-can stuff first.||||reg||6
